.TH MOUNT_CRYPTED 8 "November 2026" "mount_crypted" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
mount_crypted \- unlock LUKS devices and mount their btrfs subvolumes using remote keys
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mount_crypted
.RI [ destination ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mount_crypted
reads a list of encrypted devices from the configuration file, finds their
LUKS UUIDs on the local block devices and tries to unlock them with keys
obtained over SSH.  After all devices have been unlocked, btrfs devices are
rescanned, subvolumes are mounted and the configured services are restarted.
.PP
A key server is contacted by running
.B ssh
with its standard input connected to
.BR /dev/null .
Its output is expected to contain lines of the form
.IR UUID : key ;
the line whose UUID matches the device being unlocked is passed to
.BR cryptsetup (8).
A destination is written as
.RI [ user @] host [: port ],
with
.B 22
used when the port is omitted.  The port is probed with
.BR nmap (1)
first, unless nmap is not installed.  All destinations from the first command
line argument and from the configuration file are tried until the device is
unlocked.
.PP
If
.B KEY
is set in the environment, it is also passed to
.B cryptsetup
for every configured device.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file (default
.IR /etc/ssh_crypt )
contains one device per line:
.PP
.nf
UUID:name:service[,service...][:options[:subvol[,subvol...]]]
.fi
.PP
Lines starting with
.B #
are ignored.  Lines starting with
.B :
define additional key servers; the leading colon is stripped and the rest of
the line is split on whitespace into destinations, for example:
.PP
.nf
:keys.example.com backup@example.com:2222
.fi
.PP
Lines are read with
.B read
without the
.B -r
option: a backslash escapes the following character, and a backslash at the
end of a line continues the line on the next input line.  Write
.B \(rs\(rs
for a literal backslash.  For example, a subvolume list may be split:
.PP
.nf
12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789abc:storage:smbd:ro:\(rs
data,home
.fi
.PP
Continuation lines must not start with
.B #
or
.BR : ,
as such lines are filtered out before they are read, and they must not be
indented: whitespace on a continuation line is kept as part of the field.
.PP
The fields of a device line are:
.TP
.B UUID
LUKS UUID of the device, used to find it with
.BR blkid (8)
and to select the key from the SSH output.
.TP
.B name
Name used in the mapper device
.I MAPPER_PREFIX name _ BASENAME
and in the mount point
.IR MOUNT_DIR / name .
.TP
.B service
Comma-separated services to restart after mounting.  Each service is
restarted through
.I /etc/init.d/service
if that file is executable, and through
.B systemctl
from
.B PATH
if it is available.
.TP
.B options
Extra options for the
.B mount
command, prepended to the generated
.B subvol
option.  The single value
.B nomount
disables mounting of this device.
.TP
.B subvol
Comma-separated btrfs subvolumes to mount under
.IR MOUNT_DIR / name .
The default is
.BR @ .
The leading
.B @
is removed from the corresponding mount point directory.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DST
Space-separated destinations to try instead of those in the configuration
file.  Also taken from the first command line argument.
.TP
.B KEY
Key passed to
.B cryptsetup
for each device after the remote lookups.
.TP
.B CONFIG
Configuration file, default
.IR /etc/ssh_crypt .
.TP
.B MAPPER_DIR
Device mapper directory, default
.IR /dev/mapper .
.TP
.B MAPPER_PREFIX
Prefix of created mapper device names, default
.BR cr_ .
.TP
.B MOUNT_DIR
Parent directory of the mount points, default
.IR /mnt .
.TP
.B DEFAULT_PORT
SSH port used when a destination has no port, default
.BR 22 .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/ssh_crypt
Default configuration file.
.SH EXAMPLE
.PP
.nf
# /etc/ssh_crypt
:keys.example.com
12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789abc:storage:smbd:ro:data,home
87654321-4321-4321-4321-876543210fed:backup::nomount
.fi
.PP
Unlock the devices using a key server given on the command line (this
replaces the destinations from the configuration file):
.PP
.nf
.B mount_crypted keys2.example.com:2222
.fi
.SH SYSTEMD AND DRACUT
The package installs
.BR mount_crypted.service ,
a oneshot unit ordered before
.BR local-fs-pre.target .
It can be enabled directly or pulled in by a mount unit with
.B Requires=
and
.BR After= .
The dracut module
.B 90mount_crypted
adds the script, the configuration file and the unit to the initramfs.  It
also includes root's SSH config, known hosts and unencrypted private keys from
.I /root/.ssh
for unattended early-boot key retrieval; passphrase-protected keys are
skipped.  It is included when
.B rd.mount_crypted
is on the kernel command line, when
.I /etc/ssh_crypt
exists, or when the module is added explicitly with
.BR "dracut --add mount_crypted" .
The unit checks for
.I /etc/ssh_crypt ;
adjust its condition if
.B CONFIG
is overridden.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cryptsetup (8),
.BR btrfs (8),
.BR blkid (8),
